uthor":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix: change 3369 (d06145796e3; make verify rc=0: 21,166 + 218 passed). The parser declares --only with choices=(\"stale-channel\",) and help \"with --repair, repair only stale-channel snapshots\" (no more \"named ticket(s)\"); fsck_cli folds `--only <value>` into `--only=<value>`, so both spellings behave identically; the unknown-value error now names the one accepted value. A bare trailing --only still reports \"requires a value\". tests/unit/test_fsck_only_flag.py pins the help text and parser together (4 of 5 failed RED before the change). Choosing truthful help over per-ticket scoping: adding a per-ticket fsck filter is a feature, not this bug's fix.","timestamp":1794485047547474185},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 06:00 PST: in_progress. Change 3369 PS1 got LLM-Review -1 (blocker: `--limit N` had the same help/parse mismatch) plus 3 advisory test findings. All addressed locally in worktree .rebar/worktrees/fix-tick, amended as 804726bfd0c (same Change-Id): the fold now covers --only and --limit; tests check rendered --help, a bare --only followed by a flag, and that both spellings reach dispatch with identical values (verified failing with --limit removed from the fold). NOT yet pushed: make verify was interrupted on hand-back; re-run make verify, push PS2, reply to the 4 comments. The plan review is stale after the AC edit and LLM gates are currently blocked by the Bedrock daily spend cap (releases 16:00 PST).","timestamp":1794491813735812928},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 PST: CLOSED (class preexisting, completion signature signed). Change 3369 merged as 0b10d8df2a3 (PS2 addressed the LLM-Review findings: --limit folded too; rendered-help, bare --only, and both-spelling dispatch tests). Plan review and close ran through the worktree CLI on the Anthropic API (anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5) while the Bedrock spend cap held.","timestamp":1794524281301756001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793821910678156001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e540056b-e4bc-4059-b9bd-13993de987d9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"98bc-13ff-2f80-48ba"},{"link_uuid":"47d823ef-2a17-49d0-88f6-95e10c0bd5d9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2efe-9bb5-9a8f-4475"},{"link_uuid":"d7fba28b-1001-4b75-8f97-035a06518300","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fc23-b952-ae8b-44f0"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`rebar store fsck --help` documents `--only ONLY` as \"check only the named ticket(s)\" (`src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/repair.py:49`), but `fsck_cli` (`src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py:332-348`) accepts exactly one value, `--only=stale-channel`, and only together with `--repair`. Observed 2026-11-04 at e0bfa4e5154:\n\n- `rebar store fsck --repair-snapshots --dry-run --only 77b6-868f-f4bd-461f` -> `Error: --only requires a value` (the space-separated form documented by argparse is rejected outright).\n- `... --only=77b6-868f-f4bd-461f` -> `Error: unknown --only value '77b6-868f-f4bd-461f'`.\n\nAn operator following the help text to scope a snapshot repair to one ticket (respirable-trapezial-ekaltadeta) cannot, and has to run the whole-store pass instead.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar store fsck --help` describes `--only` as what the command actually accepts, or the command accepts what the help describes; a test pins help text and parser behaviour together.\n- [x] `--only <value>` (space-separated) and `--only=<value>` behave the same.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py","reason":"accept --only <value>; clearer error"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/repair.py","reason":"truthful --only help"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_fsck_only_flag.py","reason":"pin help and parser"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2efe-9bb5-9a8f-4475"],["relates_to","fc23-b952-ae8b-44f0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0d1f5f62-11c9-4aaf-b8b1-cab6df28e15f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e395-114c-aee9-42a5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"store fsck --help says --only takes ticket ids; the command accepts only --only=stale-channel","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f4bc7dcb-5bbf-46b1-845f-4f0f949f9ddf","f704b2da-eed5-441c-aec3-c9c5d16e0e58","e0f8d559-3ae7-45e4-8f8f-2ab58d7f38b5","47d823ef-2a17-49d0-88f6-95e10c0bd5d9","f125d35b-997e-451d-aa33-99d311000f9f","2ea84aa1-7db8-4824-bf08-d13367f39fda","091aa1fb-0cd3-4906-ad1e-78a7f8454fec","2af289a6-ca39-4c75-aea8-340644911bbc","d7fba28b-1001-4b75-8f97-035a06518300","ce7e809a-b473-4b66-82c8-7042280ffa61","0d1f5f62-11c9-4aaf-b8b1-cab6df28e15f","06c9076d-31e7-4341-9737-83fc0aef1c49","b365c4f1-e02a-495d-ac22-226b2857bfbc"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794524281301756002,"uuid":"ae962e24-0103-4ff4-859d-db9aa1b26307"}